# excel_comparer — AI agent guide

Compare `.xlsx` workbooks against a *golden* reference. Pure-Python library + thin
CLI + optional FastAPI web UI. Single runtime dep is `openpyxl`; `web` extra adds
FastAPI/Uvicorn/Jinja2.

## Architecture

Three layers, kept deliberately small and independent:

- `excel_comparer/` — the library. Import surface is fixed by `__init__.py`:
  `ExcelComparer`, `DiffCategory`, `Difference`, `format_differences`.
  - `models.py` — `DiffCategory` (StrEnum: `SHEET_MISSING|SHEET_EXTRA|VALUE|FORMAT|MERGED_CELL`)
    and the frozen `Difference` dataclass. `Difference.message` is computed per-category;
    do not store it as a field.
  - `comparer.py` — `ExcelComparer(golden_path, float_tolerance=0.0, diff_categories=...)`.
    Loads golden eagerly with `data_only=True` (cached values only, formulas are NOT inspected).
    `compare(*others)` always returns `dict[str, list[Difference]]` keyed by the original
    path string, even for a single file. Matching is strict: sheets by exact name, cells by
    coordinate (1-indexed loops over `max_row`/`max_column`).
  - `reporting.py` — `format_differences()` groups `SHEET_MISSING/EXTRA` at workbook level,
    everything else under `Sheet "<name>"`. The web UI mirrors this grouping in JS.
  - `cli.py` — argparse entry point. CLI exit code = **number of files with ≥1 diff**
    (not 0/1), see `main()`.
- `webapp/` — FastAPI app (`webapp.main:app`). Only loaded when `[web]` extra is installed.
  Saves uploads to a `tempfile.TemporaryDirectory`, instantiates `ExcelComparer` per request,
  serialises diffs via `_serialise_diff` (`asdict` + `_json_safe` stringifies non-primitives).
  Enforces `MAX_FILE_BYTES = 25 MB` and `.xlsx` only.
- `main.py` / `selftest.py` at repo root are thin runners (CLI shim and end-to-end smoke test).

## Project-specific conventions

- **Add a new format attribute** by appending to `_FORMAT_ATTRIBUTES` in `comparer.py`
  as `(dotted_path, label)`. `_get_attr_path` walks the path and returns `None` if any
  step is missing — rely on this rather than `try/except AttributeError`.
- **Adding a new `DiffCategory`** requires updates in 4 places: the enum, `Difference.message`,
  the `_compare_*` dispatch in `ExcelComparer._compare_sheet`, and the JS `renderDiffGroups`
  in `webapp/static/app.js` (which hard-codes `SHEET_MISSING`/`SHEET_EXTRA` as workbook-level).
- Empty cells: `_is_empty` treats both `None` and `""` as no-value. Format diffs are skipped
  when both sides are empty (see `_compare_sheet`).
- Float comparison uses `math.isclose(..., abs_tol=float_tolerance, rel_tol=0.0)` — absolute
  tolerance only, no relative.
- `diff_categories` is a tuple filter applied at collection time; defaults to
  `ExcelComparer.DEFAULT_DIFF_CATEGORIES = (VALUE, SHEET_MISSING, SHEET_EXTRA)`
  (FORMAT and MERGED_CELL are opt-in).
- Python target is `>=3.11` in `pyproject.toml` (floor is driven by `enum.StrEnum` and `X | Y` types).

## Developer workflows

```bash
uv sync                       # library only
uv sync --extra web           # include FastAPI/Uvicorn for the webapp
uv run python selftest.py     # end-to-end smoke test (builds temp xlsx pair)
uv run python main.py golden.xlsx other.xlsx           # CLI via shim
uv run excel-comparer golden.xlsx other.xlsx --float-tol 1e-9  # installed entry point
uv run uvicorn webapp.main:app --reload                # web UI on :8000
docker compose up --build                              # containerised web UI
```

There is **no test suite, linter, or formatter** configured. `selftest.py` is the
canonical "does it still work" check — keep it green and extend it when adding diff
categories or format attributes. The repo-root `golden.xlsx`, `other.xlsx`, `test.xlsx`
are throwaway fixtures.

## Web API contract (do not break)

`POST /api/compare` — multipart form: `golden` (file), `others` (repeatable file),
`float_tol` (float ≥ 0), `categories` (repeatable string, also accepts comma-joined).
Response shape is built in `webapp/main.py` and consumed by `webapp/static/app.js`
(`renderFileResult`, `renderDiffGroups`); changes must be made in both places.
The summary dict always contains every `DiffCategory` value plus `TOTAL`.
